{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"certifiable":true,"criteria":[{"citation":{"description":"Ticket comments (timestamps 1787856976224609473 and 1787857474063479140) name the fields (created_at, updated_at, timestamp, signed_at — time.time_ns() 19-digit integers), explain rebar emits them as bare JSON numbers outside RFC 8259 §6 interoperable range, and explain that GitHub Copilot CLI's wasm-bindgen bridge materializes them as BigInt which throws on JSON.stringify.","kind":"source"},"criterion":"The failing field is named, and the reason it becomes a JS `BigInt` in the client is stated. Verify: a ticket comment names the field(s) whose value exceeds the JS safe-integer range and explains the wire type rebar emits plus the client-side parse that produces `BigInt`.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"description":"js_safe_result() and install_js_safe_guard() implement the fix; live validation comment confirms SUCCESS with no BigInt error.","kind":"file","line_end":280,"line_start":1,"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py"},"criterion":"`list_tickets` with `{\"status\":\"open\",\"ticket_type\":\"epic\"}` returns a ticket list with no serialization error.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"description":"Same guard applies to all tools; live validation confirms 76 rows, 0 bare integers outside JS-safe range.","kind":"file","line_end":280,"line_start":1,"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py"},"criterion":"`ready_tickets` returns a ticket list with no serialization error.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":150,"line_start":118,"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_js_safe_integers.py"},"criterion":"An MCP-layer regression test exercises `list_tickets` with these filters. Verify: the test exists, fails when the guard is disabled, and passes with it enabled.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"description":"All three schemas declare signed_at as [\"integer\",\"string\"]; common.schema.json declares timestamp and source_created_at as [\"integer\",\"string\",\"null\"]; structural guard test at test_mcp_js_safe_integers.py:201-231.","kind":"file","line_end":20,"line_start":1,"path":"src/rebar/schemas/sign_result.schema.json"},"criterion":"The tool's own advertised `outputSchema` accepts the widened wire form. created_at/updated_at/last_reopened_at/source_created_at (ticket_state.schema.json), comments[].timestamp/comments[].source_created_at (common.schema.json) and signed_at (sign_result, verify_signature_result, plan_review_status schemas) each declare `\"type\": [\"integer\",\"string\"]`, and the three signed_at annotations in _mcp_models.py widen to `int | str`.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"description":"Final ticket comment (timestamp 1787892705975347001) by RebarBotNava records first-hand call against https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp, OAuth-authenticated, showing created_at: '1786649271159032001' and updated_at: '1787174253995137001' as strings, with int('1786649271159032001') == 1786649271159032001 (exact round-trip).","kind":"source"},"criterion":"[non-codebase] `list_tickets` with `{\"status\":\"open\",\"ticket_type\":\"epic\"}` returns through a LOSSLESS-parsing JS client against the deployed endpoint with no BigInt serialization error AND with every ns timestamp arriving as an exact decimal string.","kind":"non-codebase","met":true},{"citation":{"description":"Same final comment records ready_tickets: 76 rows, 939,719 chars, BARE integers outside JS-safe range: 0, decimal-STRING ns timestamps: 235, with exact round-trip verified.","kind":"source"},"criterion":"[non-codebase] `ready_tickets` returns through that same lossless-parsing client against that deployed endpoint with no BigInt serialization error AND with every ns timestamp arriving as an exact decimal string.","kind":"non-codebase","met":true},{"citation":{"description":"Final comment confirms container rebar-mcp-6fe5c0d54574-8093 at https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp serving main at/after 6fe5c0d54574 which contains fix commit bdfb9b3115c5ad29a685e04e71f5dce0e2ac21cc ('Emit JS-safe integers on the MCP wire'), verified via git merge-base --is-ancestor.","kind":"source"},"criterion":"[non-codebase] The deployed container is confirmed to be serving the build that carries the fix.","kind":"non-codebase","met":true},{"citation":{"description":"js_safe_result() recursively converts out-of-range integers to decimal strings; install_js_safe_guard() wraps all MCP tools. Live validation confirms zero bare integers outside JS-safe range in deployed responses. Both tools return well-formed results with timestamps as exact decimal strings.","kind":"file","line_end":280,"line_start":1,"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py"},"criterion":"Bug 'rebar-list_tickets MCP tool call fails with TypeError: Do not know how to serialize a BigInt' is actually resolved: the reported defect no longer reproduces and expected behavior holds.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true}],"findings":[],"material_fingerprint":null,"metrics":{"alias_index_build_ms":829,"commits_inspected":2801,"descendant_ids":0,"descendant_scope_ms":1784,"det_ms":4964.6,"diff_validation_ms":141,"distinct_references":2337,"git_history_read_ms":253,"landing_check_ms":1256,"llm_calls":1,"llm_ms":119844.2,"material_policy_ms":0,"pre_verifier_total_ms":5069,"referencing_commits_found":1,"requests":12,"structural_scan_ms":1961,"ticket_ref_resolution_ms":27,"tool_calls":11,"total_ms":124859.1,"verifier_annotation_ms":0,"verifier_attempt_count":1,"verifier_attempt_setup_ms":0,"verifier_attempts_ms":281243,"verifier_between_attempts_ms":0,"verifier_build_drift_ms":316,"verifier_call_ms":281271,"verifier_code_snapshot_